            <ArticleTitle>Relation of lumen size to restenosis after percutaneous transluminal coronary balloon angioplasty. Lovastatin Restenosis Trial Group.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>221-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The relation between post-percutaneous transluminal balloon angioplasty (post-PTCA) and angiography indexes were investigated in the Lovastatin Restenosis Trial. Post-PTCA percent diameter measured by the operator was found to be a weak predictor of angiographic and clinical follow-up restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
